{
  "schema": "trial/1",
  "trial": "P-58",
  "question": "Does a pull request's `lastEditedAt` move when its description is edited, and not when only its title is, or when its head is pushed; and does an edit by a bot or an App move it?",
  "pass": "Written 2026-11-03T19:18:38Z, before anything runs (issue 519, its first box, at the next free P-number). On a new canary pull request opened by the Maintainer's login with a description that mentions an issue bare, GraphQL's lastEditedAt, editor and userContentEdits on the pull request are read after it opens, then after each of four changes made in turn: its title alone edited; its description edited, the bare mention turned into a closing keyword; a push to its head; and its description edited by a workflow's GITHUB_TOKEN, as a bot. Pass if lastEditedAt moves, and userContentEdits gains an edit naming its editor, on each description edit, the bot's included, and on neither the title-only edit nor the push; fail otherwise, each read recorded. Whether the reader App's token reads them the same is not asked here: that needs its key at the Maintainer's terminal, and is owed. Run on 2026-11-03 on canary pull request 95, opened, edited, pushed to, labelled and closed by the Maintainer's login, its branch, its workflow file and the label deleted after (writes not recorded here); the bot's edit is workflow run 41702406280. Passed. At once after it opened, lastEditedAt was null and userContentEdits empty. Twenty-three seconds after it opened, the cubic App edited the description, adding its own block: lastEditedAt became that time, editor cubic-dev-ai, a Bot, and userContentEdits held two, the opening text by don-petry and cubic's. The title-only edit changed neither. The description's edit, See #51 turned into Closes #51, moved lastEditedAt to its time, editor don-petry, a User, and added an edit. The push changed neither. CodeRabbit then edited the description, two minutes after the push, adding its own summary, and the workflow's bot edited it: lastEditedAt moved to the bot's edit, editor github-actions, a Bot, and userContentEdits held five, each naming its editor; a minute later the same. So lastEditedAt marks every description edit, a reviewer App's own included, and editor names only the last: a person's edit after an approval is told apart from an App's only by userContentEdits.",
